RunInfo: 'Drell-Yan events with $Z \to ee$ or $Z \to \mu\mu$ and at least one AK8
  jet. Generate with a jet $p_\mathrm{T}$ threshold well below 200 GeV so the
  first measured $p_\mathrm{T}$ slice is not sculpted.'
Beams: [p+, p+]
Energies: [13000]
Luminosity_fb: 138
Description:
  'Normalized differential distributions of $\log_{10}(\rho^2)$, where
  $\rho = m / (p_\mathrm{T} R)$ for the anti-$k_\mathrm{T}$ $R = 0.8$ jet
  recoiling against a Z boson, measured separately for the ungroomed jet mass and
  the soft-drop groomed jet mass ($\beta = 0$, $z_\mathrm{cut} = 0.1$), in three
  slices of ungroomed jet $p_\mathrm{T}$: [200, 290], [290, 400] and
  [400, $\infty$) GeV. Distributions are normalized to unit area within each
  $p_\mathrm{T}$ slice.

  Fiducial selection: exactly two same-flavour opposite-sign dressed leptons
  (electrons $p_\mathrm{T} > 40$ GeV, muons $p_\mathrm{T} > 29$ GeV,
  $|\eta| < 2.4$, dressing cone $\Delta R = 0.1$) and no additional lepton
  passing those cuts; $p_\mathrm{T}(Z) > 90$ GeV; $71 < m_{\ell\ell} < 111$ GeV.
  AK8 jets with $|y| < 2.4$ are cleaned of dressed leptons within
  $\Delta R < 0.4$. The leading cleaned jet is required to satisfy
  $\Delta\phi(Z, \mathrm{jet}) > 1.57$ and a $p_\mathrm{T}$ asymmetry
  $|p_\mathrm{T}^Z - p_\mathrm{T}^\mathrm{jet}| /
  (p_\mathrm{T}^Z + p_\mathrm{T}^\mathrm{jet}) < 0.3$, and is the measured jet;
  the event is rejected if that jet fails the topology requirement.

  The 2D histograms zjets_{ungroomed,groomed} carry the absolute fiducial cross
  section in the reference ($p_\mathrm{T}$, $\log_{10}(\rho^2)$) binning; the
  corresponding _slice0/1/2 histograms are the per-slice unit-area distributions
  that are directly comparable to the measurement.'
Keywords: [zjet, jet mass, jet substructure, soft drop, grooming]
